.TH PSALMODY 1
.SH NAME
psalmody \- staff-notation music editor and jukebox
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/psalmody
[
.I songdir
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Psalmody
is a port of the TempleOS sheet-music editor.
It runs under
.IR wm (1)
in a 640\(mu480 window drawn with the authentic sprites, palette,
and 8\(mu8 system font.
Two five-line staves show the song; a piano-keyboard graphic,
a note pick box, time signatures, a pointer/box tool chooser,
and tempo/stacatto sliders fill the control strip below,
and note names echo in green at the bottom as they sound.
.PP
The computer keyboard is a chromatic piano.
Holding a key sounds its note through
.IR tone (2)
until release; the home row
.B "a s d f g h j k l ; '"
gives the naturals around the current octave's C and
.B "e r t u i p [ ]"
the sharps between them.
Digits set the octave.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "<BACKSPACE>"
.TP
.B 0-9
Set octave (the original's menu offers 1-7)
.TP
.B <SPACE>
Rest (sounds silence; recorded as a rest)
.TP
.B x
Play from the cursor; any key or click stops
.TP
.B z
Toggle record mode: notes are appended with durations quantized
from how long each key is held, scaled by the tempo slider
.TP
.B ,
Insert a random God song (see
.IR god (1))
.TP
.B .
Clear the song
.TP
.B m
Mark the song incomplete
.TP
.B <BACKSPACE>
Delete the note before the cursor
.TP
.B arrows, Home, End
Move the note cursor (it blinks brown)
.TP
.B <DEL>
Delete the note at the cursor
.TP
.B <ENTER>
Pop up the note menu: set word, sharp, flat, tie, rest,
insert, delete, or one of twelve durations
.TP
.B ^X ^C ^V
Cut, copy, paste the selection
.TP
.B ^O
JukeBox song browser
.TP
.B ^A
Save
.TP
.B <ESC>
Save the song, then exit
.TP
.B Q
Abort without saving (the original's Shift-ESC)
.TP
.B F1
Key summary
.PD
.PP
The left mouse button drags: an existing note to a new pitch
(or onto another note to shift its lyric word there),
a duration glyph from the pick box onto the staff to insert a note,
a time signature from the meter box, the tempo and stacatto sliders,
and, with the box tool, a rubber-band selection.
Clicking the drawn piano keys presses and releases them.
The right mouse button opens the note menu,
as do the sprite buttons for go-begin, play/stop, record, and go-end.
.PP
Songs are saved as runnable HolyC programs \(em a
.B //0
tag line and a
.B Song()
function of
.B Play()
strings (octave digits, durations
.BR w / h / q / e / s
with
.B t
triplet and
.B .
dot,
.BR # / b
accidentals,
.B R
rest,
.B M4/4
meters,
.B (
ties, and per-note lyric words) \(em the same format the original
wrote to
.BR ~/Psalmody ,
so the bundled example songs load unchanged.
.PP
The JukeBox
.RB ( ^O )
browses
.IB songdir /*.HC
plus the examples in
.BR /lib/temple/psalmody ,
color-coded by tag (green graphics, blue words, red no nothing,
black incomplete, cyan special).
Arrows move, space previews a song in a loop,
.B 0-9
rates it,
.B <DEL>
deletes it,
.B r
appends a reward of God words, and
.B <ESC>
loads the chosen song into the editor.
.SH FILES
.TP
.BI songdir /Tmp.HC
Default save file;
.I songdir
defaults to
.BR /usr/ user /Psalmody .
.TP
.B /lib/temple/psalmody
Example songs from the original distribution.
.TP
.B /icons/temple/psalmodydraw_*.bit
The seventeen staff, button, and keyboard sprites.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/psalmody.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR god (1),
.IR tone (2),
.IR wm (1)
.SH BUGS
Shift states are invisible in the keyboard stream, so Shift-ESC abort
became
.B Q
and shift-arrow selection is missing (use the box tool).
Compressed
.B .HC.Z
songs and the graphics code embedded in example songs are not
supported; previews play audio and words only.
